docs/AI_DEVELOPMENT_LOG.md:137:In an isolated worktree based on preparation commit `4f985f2`, added opt-in sanitized transport categorization, independent customer-text safety verification with fail-closed errors, bounded financial context, a narrow stored-assertion correction path, singleton draft selection, and deterministic tests. A separate recorded-result test evaluated the first three live outputs through policy and action. The 19-request synthetic run (one transport plus 18 semantic calls) found a safe rejection for the gross correction, an evidence failure on one opt-out attempt and a false COST objection on its repeat. The original three case actions were appropriate in the observed runs, but this is not proof of reliability. Blocker lifecycle requires the documented CCR; F-01 remains PARTIALLY FIXED. Details and evidence are in `docs/evaluation/F01_TRUST_BOUNDARIES_EVALUATION.md`. No contract, fixture, push, merge or external business effect was made.
docs/AI_DEVELOPMENT_LOG.md:141:Worked in the existing `codex/f01-trust-boundaries` worktree at `09001b7`, retaining the pre-existing uncommitted structured extraction prompt experiment. The local configured model and the supplied acceptance artifacts identify `gpt-5.4-mini`; this task made no model requests. The prior artifacts report differing extractor/verifier labels, verifier-only TIME, invalid amount carry-over and conflicting corrected amounts. Updated the prompt guidance, conservatively hold unilateral noncritical findings rather than persisting them, and added narrow evidence-aware correction and repeated-text handling. Original assertions and blocker lifecycle remain intact; uncertainty remains when correction targets cannot be identified. Added focused deterministic tests without changing datasets, canonical fixtures, or shared contracts.
docs/AI_DEVELOPMENT_LOG.md:143:Final local checks: `pnpm lint`, `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm test` (155 passed / 3 skipped), `pnpm build`, `pnpm dataset:validate`, and `git diff --check` passed. The 24-case command selection was checked with `--dry-run` only. These results do not establish semantic correctness: routine-question disagreements can still hold analysis, location/debt attribution is model-dependent, and amount/basis correction is deliberately narrow. Independent model evaluation and the existing blocker lifecycle CCR remain open; U0 is not declared complete.
docs/AI_DEVELOPMENT_LOG.md:147:In the existing `codex/f01-trust-boundaries` worktree at `bc2d8fa`, separated independent protected-signal discovery from review of proposed commercial objections. The internal review accepts cited explanations for unsupported commercial candidates; unresolved sensitive disagreements remain safe failures, and existing persisted blockers are not closed. R07 now handles ordinary objections while TRUST and privacy remain protected handoffs. Added deterministic adapter and policy regressions. `pnpm lint`, `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm test` (160 passed, 3 skipped), `pnpm build`, `pnpm dataset:validate`, and `git diff --check` passed. No paid model run was made; real-model acceptance and the existing blocker lifecycle CCR remain open.
docs/evaluation/F01_OPENAI_REMEDIATION.md:142:**Dictamen: PARTIALLY FIXED; no listo para integración.** Se añadió un verificador separado, proyección acotada de contexto financiero, diagnósticos de transporte y selección determinista de plantilla única. La evaluación real usó 19 solicitudes en total, incluida una comprobación de transporte. Los originales produjeron acciones apropiadas en esta muestra, pero la corrección de base falló de forma segura, una prueba de opt-out falló por evidencia y su repetición generó un COST falso. Los bloqueos antiguos siguen sin una vía auditada de retractación; se preparó un CCR sin modificar contratos. Resultados, límites, pruebas e instrumentos en [F01_TRUST_BOUNDARIES_EVALUATION.md](F01_TRUST_BOUNDARIES_EVALUATION.md).
