docs/implementation/tasks/F01_TRUST_BOUNDARIES.md:12:This brief authorizes Codex to implement and test the listed changes locally in an isolated branch/worktree, using existing `OPENAI_API_KEY` and **exact** configured `OPENAI_MODEL` for a bounded synthetic-data evaluation. Never print/log/commit secrets. No external messaging, appointments, CRM, financial approvals, Notion work, or real customer data. **No merge or push to `main` without explicit user authorization.** Follow `AGENTS.md`; if a public shared-contract change is genuinely necessary, produce a Contract Change Request (CCR) and stop only the affected task until approved. Do not silently modify `src/contracts/**`, canonical `src/config/**`, or `src/fixtures/**` to force a pass.
docs/implementation/tasks/F01_TRUST_BOUNDARIES.md:39:Implement structured, privacy-safe internal diagnostic categories: DNS/network/TLS, 401/403 authentication, 429 rate or quota, 400/422 request/schema errors, 5xx provider, timeout/abort, incomplete/refusal, parse/schema, semantic validation. Where available, retain provider status/error code/request ID in a sanitized **server-only diagnostic**; do not echo raw messages, request bodies, API keys, headers, or complete model outputs to the UI. Public `ApplicationError` should remain stable unless a CCR is approved. Guard logs behind a local opt-in diagnostic flag and redact.
