docs/evaluation/F01_TRUST_BOUNDARIES_EVALUATION.md:29:The implementation does not yet establish a safe auditable lifecycle for legacy model blockers: existing blockers are merged and cannot carry verified invalidation/resolution evidence through `Interpretation`. See [CCR](F01_BLOCKER_LIFECYCLE_CCR.md). No existing genuine protected blocker is automatically cleared merely because a subsequent model omits it; that conservative behavior also leaves legacy false positives sticky. The stored-context correction handling is narrow and does not reliably cover model omissions or paraphrases, as C01 demonstrates. Two amounts/subjects and general field-level semantic grounding remain insufficiently independently verified. The verifier can itself make false classifications; matching a second call does not establish truth. Quoted text remains required, not sufficient.

